AID TOKEN CHOOSE-TESTS
ATITLE CDATA Choose Expression Tests
(SUITE
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-EXPRESSIONS
ATITLE CDATA Choose Expressions
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Choose expressions pattern match on union types, allowing different code paths based on which variant is present.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-ON-VARIANTS
ATITLE CDATA Choose on Variant Construction
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Choose can match directly on constructed variants.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-MATCH-SOME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option union(Some: int, None)\nchoose Option.Some(7): when v: Some: v else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-7\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-MATCH-NONE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option union(Some: int, None)\nchoose Option.None: when v: Some: v else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-0\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-BINDING
ATITLE CDATA Choose with Binding
(TESTS
(PROSE
-When a variant carries a value, the value can be bound to a name.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-BIND-VALUE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union(Ok: int, Err: int)\nchoose Result.Ok(42): when x: Ok: x + 1 else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-43\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-MULTIPLE-WHEN
ATITLE CDATA Multiple When Clauses
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Choose can have multiple when clauses to match different variants.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-MULTI-MATCH-FIRST
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union(Ok: int, Err: int)\nchoose Result.Ok(10): when x: Ok: x when e: Err: e + 100
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN CHOOSE-MULTI-MATCH-SECOND
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union(Ok: int, Err: int)\nchoose Result.Err(5): when x: Ok: x when e: Err: e + 100
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-105\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN OPTIONAL-TYPES
ATITLE CDATA Optional Types
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Optional types use null pointer optimization (NPO) for efficient representation.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN IS-NULL-CHECK
ATITLE CDATA Is Null Check
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The is null expression checks if an optional value is None.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN IS-NULL-NONE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\nfunction check(x: int?) returns int: if x is null: 0 else 1\ncheck(Option[int].None)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-0\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN IS-NULL-SOME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\nfunction check(x: int?) returns int: if x is null: 0 else 1\ncheck(Option[int].Some(42))
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-1\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN OPTIONAL-SUGAR
ATITLE CDATA Optional Type Sugar
(TESTS
(PROSE
-T? is syntactic sugar for Option[T].\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN OPTIONAL-SUGAR-UNWRAP
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\nfunction unwrap(x: int?) returns int: choose x: when v: Some: v else 0\nunwrap(Option[int].Some(42))
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN GENERIC-OPTION
ATITLE CDATA Generic Option Types
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Generic unions like Option[T] work with choose for pattern matching.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN GENERIC-OPTION-SOME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\nchoose Option[int].Some(42): when v: Some: v else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN GENERIC-OPTION-NONE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\nchoose Option[int].None: when v: Some: v else -1
)INPUT
(EXPECT
--1\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN VARIANT-CONSTRUCTION
ATITLE CDATA Variant Construction
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Union variants can be constructed explicitly using Type.Variant syntax.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN VARIANT-CONSTRUCT
ATITLE CDATA Construct Variants
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Variants are constructed with Type.Variant(value) syntax.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN VARIANT-OK
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union: (Ok: int, Error: int)\nchoose Result.Ok(42): when x: Ok: x else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN VARIANT-ERROR
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union: (Ok: int, Error: int)\nchoose Result.Error(100): when e: Error: e else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-100\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN VARIANT-IS
ATITLE CDATA Variant Is Expression
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The is expression tests if a union value matches a variant.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN VARIANT-IS-OK
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union: (Ok: int, Error: int)\nif Result.Ok(50) is Ok : 1 else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-1\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN VARIANT-IS-NOT-MATCH
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union: (Ok: int, Error: int)\nif Result.Error(33) is Ok : 1 else 0
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-0\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
)SUITE
C
